{sentence}
Color gamut refers to the range of colors that a particular device can produce or record.
{sentence}
The color gamut of a monitor is shown in a triangular area enclosed by the color coordinates of the monitor's red, green, and blue colors.
{sentence}
A chromaticity diagram with different color gamuts is shown in Figure 1.
{sentence}
Commonly seen color gamut standards include NTSC, sRGB, AdobeRGB, DCI-P3, EBU, and AppleRGB.
{sentence}
The selection of color gamut really depends on your workflow and requirements.
